  body: "# AIP reporting: historical boundary\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed. No
    entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured introduction defines an AIP as fixing retirement
    provision subject to deemed increases, then records that no new AIPs are set on or after 6.4.16 and
    links that change to reporting relevant circumstances.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 83000, PDF
    page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5aa9038ee5274a3e391e3e7c/dmgch83.pdf#page=3)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `b7b36dae645ea1886638833a099c6eccf6a2f1312c1e2708fa1de7bd8a63e43e`.\n\
    \nThis is a source-stated historical boundary, not independent verification of current law. Much of
    chapter 83 has damaged letter spacing; deeper modelling is recorded as a gap.\n\nThe capture date,
    the publication page's update date and a date stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked
    legislation and memos need their own provision, version and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/assessed-income-period
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The definition and accompanying note expressly connect the historical AIP arrangement
      with the reporting boundary. The association retains the note instead of treating old
      AIP-setting instructions as current.
    evidence:
    - page: page/83/0003
      quote: "83000   An assessed income period (AIP) is a period specified by a DM during which the\n\
        \        amount of a claimant’s retirement provision is fixed subject to deemed increases\n  \
        \                                                           1\n        made in accordance with
        the relevant legislation .\n                                                                 \
        \                      1SPCAct02,s7(4)\n\n                                                   \
        \           1\n        Note: No new AIPs will be set on, or after 6.4.16 . As a consequence, claimants
        will\n        be expected to report all relevant changes in their circumstances, including their\n\
        \        retirement provision. Accompanying changes to existing, fixed period and some\n     \
        \   indefinite period AIPs are described in this chapter.\n                           1PensionsAct14,s28;PensionsAct2014(CommencementNo.5)Order2015.s2(2)(b)"
      locator: DMG 83000
